{
  "configuration_id": "config_021",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_001 (multimodal, multiprofile, scvi_n200, resnet50, transformer, concat) achieved the best accuracy at 0.688, a large jump over singleprofile (0.536) and image-only (0.208), confirming that multiprofile + transformer aggregation is the key architectural driver. The remaining question is whether the image modality can contribute more signal with a stronger encoder. This experiment tests imagenet_vit_l in place of resnet50 while holding all other settings (scvi_n200, transformer aggregation, concat fusion, multiprofile) identical to config_001, isolating the image-encoder effect. It is the best next use of the budget because (a) it is the most informative single-variable extension of the current best, (b) ViT-L offers substantially more representational capacity than ResNet50 for the image branch, making it the most likely lever to push accuracy above 0.688, and (c) if it fails to improve, we confirm resnet50 is sufficient and can redirect remaining experiments to fusion or RNA-encoder variants. Expected relative cost: moderately higher than config_001 (~7–8 GPU hrs vs 5.16) due to the larger ViT-L backbone, but justified by the potential accuracy gain."
}

